{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfBVikbuefDtHv8urJcvc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnosis, without host data (I don't run commands):\n\n**Severity: warning.** 91% is above the usual 80–85% alert line but not yet at the 95%+ point where writes fail, journald stops, or Prometheus/Loki WAL breaks. Treat as \"act today\", not \"page now\".\n\n**Likely causes, in order for a homelab host like x:**\n- Journal or log growth. Check `journalctl --disk-usage` and `/var/log`. Vector shipping nothing (the NOFILE 1024 issue) can leave local logs piling up.\n- Container image and layer sprawl. Docker or Proxmox CT/VM disks, unpruned images, dangling volumes.\n- Snapshots or backups landing on the root filesystem instead of the intended dataset.\n- TSDB retention. Prometheus, Loki, or Grafana data outrunning retention settings.\n- A runaway file. One process writing a core dump, crash log, or tmp file.\n\n**Next step:** `du -xhd1 /` then `ncdu` on the largest branch, and check inode use too. Confirm the growth rate from Grafana before deleting anything. If it's flat, it's a one-time fill and there's time. If it's climbing, find the writer first.\n\nNot verified against the host. Confidence is low until someone runs those checks."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33081,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33081},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6af16283-e1ed-4c7b-8a42-e7ac53186635","uuid":"92c04ebe-da6f-4f92-8e27-a758f0bdaa49","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:58:09.895Z","request_id":"req_011CfBVijtVcspfUYFGzAwrr"}
